pipelines.recommendedVamsSchema:
ONE pipeline + ONE workflow + N templates (one per target format).

pipeline.json: { pipelineId: "conversion-3d-basic", pipelineName: "3D Basic Format Conversion", category: "conversion", description: "Convert 3D mesh files between formats (STL, OBJ, PLY, GLTF, GLB, 3MF, XAML, 3DXML, DAE, XYZ) using the Trimesh library.", systemConfig: { inputFileArity: "one", assetScope: { singleAssetOnly: true, wholeAssetAllowed: false, folderAllowed: false, crossAssetAllowed: false }, metadataInputs: { assetMetadata: false, fileMetadata: false, fileAttributes: false }, requireTemplate: true, allowCustomTemplateOverride: true, auxPreviewPipelineSuffix: "", inputFileFilters: { allow: [".stl",".obj",".ply",".gltf",".glb",".3mf",".xaml",".3dxml",".dae",".xyz"], exclude: [] } }, executionConfig: { executionType: "Lambda", waitForCallback: "Disabled", taskTimeout: "900", taskHeartbeatTimeout: "", lambda: {} /* resourceId injected by CDK resourceOverrides.lambdaName */ } }

DECISION — templates are per-TO (output) format, NOT per from->to. The engine auto-detects the input format, so there is no from-dimension in the code; a from->to matrix would be artificial and multiply templates ~10x for no behavioral difference. Author one template per output format:
 templates/to-obj.json: { templateId: "to-obj", templateName: "Convert to OBJ", configFormat: "json", configBody: "{\"outputType\": \".obj\"}", tagSchema: [] }
 templates/to-stl.json: { templateId: "to-stl", templateName: "Convert to STL", configFormat: "json", configBody: "{\"outputType\": \".stl\"}", tagSchema: [] }
 templates/to-gltf.json: { templateId: "to-gltf", ... configBody: "{\"outputType\": \".gltf\"}" }
 templates/to-glb.json: { templateId: "to-glb", ... configBody: "{\"outputType\": \".glb\"}" } (keep the original 4 to preserve behavior; optionally add .ply/.3mf/.dae/.xyz as extra templates since the engine already supports them).
ALTERNATIVE if per-run selection is desired instead of per-template: a SINGLE template with tagSchema:[{tagKey:"outputType", type:"enum", required:true, default:".glb", enumValues:[".obj",".stl",".gltf",".glb",".ply",".3mf",".dae",".xyz"]}] and configBody "{\"outputType\": \"{{outputType}}\"}". Recommend the per-template layout for parity with today's 4 discrete registrations plus optionally the enum template for flexibility.

workflow.json: { workflowId: "conversion-3d-basic", workflowName: "3D Basic Format Conversion", category: "conversion", systemConfig: { inputFileArity: "one", concurrencyRestriction: "none", metadataInputs: {assetMetadata:false,fileMetadata:false,fileAttributes:false} }, triggers: [] }. Do NOT set a fileUpload trigger by default — the V1 CRs all passed autoTriggerOnFileExtensionsUpload:"" (no auto-trigger), and auto-triggering an ambiguous target format is wrong. Leave triggers empty; templates are chosen per manual execution. (If a trigger is later wanted it needs a defaultTemplateIds entry picking one target format.)
